# Copy to .env and adjust. .env is gitignored, so nothing set there travels with the code.

# Which sign-in the app offers, read in the development project and nowhere else: production
# and staging are pinned in src/lib/auth/auth-mode.ts, which is the only place the mode is
# decided. Normally comes from apphosting.development.yaml, so set it here only to override.
#
# `fake` swaps Entra ID for a dialog that mints a session from a typed name and role, so the
# app can be tried as several teachers and students without tenant accounts. It provisions
# real Auth accounts and real user records, which is why a project that was never named gets
# the real sign-in whatever this says.
# AUTH_MODE=fake

# The one thing this file is still needed for. Minting a custom token means signing a JWT, and
# the user credential from `gcloud auth application-default login` holds no signing key, so the
# Admin SDK signs through the IAM API instead and has to be told which account to sign as.
# Deployments discover this from the metadata server and must leave it unset.
#
# Grant yourself the right to sign as it once (development only -- never for staging or
# production, where nobody needs to mint tokens from a laptop):
#   gcloud iam service-accounts add-iam-policy-binding \
#     firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc@htld-sportsweek-development.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
#     --member="user:YOUR_EMAIL" --role="roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator" \
#     --project=htld-sportsweek-development
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_ID=firebase-adminsdk-fbsvc@htld-sportsweek-development.iam.gserviceaccount.com
